I also found the IPVV README explicitly describing the higher synthesis path C1 → THEMES → ESSAYS → EDUCATION, and saying the earlier essay-rich C1 material was preserved as essay assets. The current default branch does not expose that legacy directory through GitHub's contents API, so I have not invented material I could not retrieve. I likewise couldn't locate a current object literally named “LogicVids”; the Pāṭala source registry itself is excellent and explicitly indexes machine-readable Tantrāloka, IPVV, Tantrasāra, Spanda and related sources through GRETIL, Sanskrit & Trika Śaivism, Mahānaya and others.

The Re-rendering Atlas is already remarkably close to the practical architecture we need. Its daimon section has daily oath/invocation, repeated contact, union, charge, dream seeding, immediate dream recording, staged Acher practice, extended Corbin/Proclus/Iamblichus material and a synthesized Daimon Path.

Here is the canonical synthesis I would now use.

THE SVĀTANTRYA PROTOCOL
Recognition, Imagination, Will and the Deliberate Construction of a Life
A longitudinal N=1 experiment in consciousness, agency and manifestation
I. THE PURPOSE

This system begins with one proposition taken seriously enough to organize a life around it:

Consciousness may possess a greater creative participation in reality than the ordinary model of an isolated mind observing an independently finished world allows.

The experiment does not begin by claiming this proposition has been scientifically established.

It begins by asking:

If it were true, how should a human being actually live?

Not occasionally.

Not while making a vision board.

Not through desperate wishing.

Every day.

The experimental subject fixes one concrete life-world in advance and then attempts to bring the whole aperture of life—attention, imagination, affect, belief, identity, behavior, skill, resources and circumstance—into increasing coherence with it.

For the present experiment the terminal world is frozen separately in the Life90 system.

The practical criterion is deliberately brutal:

Did the frozen target become the subject's ordinary lived world by the terminal date?

YES or NO.

Deviation may subsequently be analyzed.

It may not redefine the original outcome.

The research question is therefore not:

Can I reinterpret whatever happens as manifestation?

It is:

What happens when a human being recognizes consciousness as creative, specifies one world with unusual precision, repeatedly inhabits that world imaginally, organizes behavior around it for years, and records the complete trajectory?

II. THE EPISTEMIC CONTRACT

Taking a metaphysical hypothesis seriously does not mean protecting it from failure.

It means giving it the strongest possible implementation.

The experiment therefore maintains four registers.

Register A — Tradition

What Abhinavagupta, Utpaladeva, Seth, Bashar, Ra, Crowley, Monroe, Rowe, Corbin, Selig, Kepple, Ziewe and other sources actually claim.

These claims are preserved as claims.

Register B — Working ontology

The metaphysical model provisionally adopted for practice.

This is the world-picture from which the experimenter acts.

Register C — Phenomenology

What was actually experienced:

imagery;
bodily states;
insight;
autonomous-seeming images;
dreams;
recognition states;
changes in desire;
synchronicity experiences;
intuitive prompts.

An experience is recorded because it happened, not because its interpretation is known.

Register D — Outcome

Externally checkable events:

income;
savings;
language competence;
contacts;
property research;
travel;
skills acquired;
offers;
opportunities;
purchases;
residence;
animals;
objective features of the terminal life.

These registers are never collapsed.

Experience is evidence that an experience occurred.
It is not automatically evidence for its strongest metaphysical interpretation.

That rule is borrowed directly from the discipline already present in the IPVV project: distinguish the felt from the ground and do not silently promote an interpretive synthesis into textual or demonstrative evidence.

III. THE PRIMARY ONTOLOGY: RECOGNITION
1. Nothing new is acquired

The IPVV project's own condensed thesis should become the foundation of the entire praxis:

Recognition is re-cognition.

What changes is not the production of a new Self but the positioning from which the already-present Self is apprehended.

Your IPVV work identifies three forms of the same movement:

foregrounding → “I was never not” → enjoyed union.

The phenomenal contents need not disappear.

The finite person need not disappear.

What changes is the status assigned to that finite standpoint.

This immediately separates Recognition from ego inflation.

The practice is not:

Thomas Prior, biography and personality, is an omnipotent supernatural individual.

The stronger Śaiva proposition is:

The consciousness appearing here is not ontologically external to the power through which appearing itself occurs.

The aperture remains localized.

Localization is no longer automatically interpreted as ultimate separation.

That is the σ-flip.

IV. VIMARŚA: WHY CONSCIOUSNESS IS NOT A MIRROR

The IPVV synthesis places enormous weight on vimarśa.

Bare luminosity—prakāśa without reflexive self-apprehension—would be inert like a crystal.

Consciousness does not merely illuminate.

It knows that it illuminates.

It appropriates what appears as its experience.

The IPVV work reconstructs Abhinavagupta's identifications:

vimarśa = parā-vāk
vimarśa = sphurattā / pulsation
vimarśa = māheśvarya / Lordship

and connects this with an epistemology of agency.

This matters enormously.

If consciousness were merely passive illumination, manifestation would be philosophically anomalous.

If reflexive self-determination is intrinsic to consciousness, creative agency is no longer imported from somewhere else.

It belongs to what consciousness is.

V. SVĀTANTRYA

The central operative term is therefore:

SVĀTANTRYA — FREEDOM

Not freedom in the political sense.

Not the ability of an ego to demand arbitrary outcomes.

It is the spontaneous self-determining capacity attributed to Śiva-consciousness.

The experiment's strongest Śaiva axiom becomes:

[
\text{Consciousness} \neq \text{passive witness}
]

but rather:

\text{illumination}
+
\text{self-apprehension}
+
\text{self-determination}
]

Finite existence is then a constrained or aperture-localized expression of this capacity.

Recognition therefore means:

I cease treating agency as something exercised by an ontologically powerless observer trapped inside an alien world.

The practical question changes from:

“How can I force reality to give me X?”

to:

“What determinate expression is this aperture choosing, and how completely can every level of its operation become congruent with that expression?”

VI. DIFFERENCE IS NOT THE ENEMY

One of the most useful insights in the IPVV translation notes is the bhedābheda frame:

the one enters the many; difference and non-difference need not contradict one another; conventional reality is not simply dismissed as fiction.

This prevents an enormous spiritual error.

If the physical world is a real articulation of consciousness, then:

earning money;
learning Hindi;
lifting weights;
finding land;
learning animal husbandry;
understanding Indian bureaucracy;
developing relationships;
negotiating;
building;
repairing;
saving;
acquiring tools;

are not embarrassingly “mundane” activities contaminating a spiritual act.

They are manifestations of the same operation at the level of kriyā.

Matter is not something to circumvent.

It is where the Will becomes specific.

Crowley's wonderfully concrete definition of Magick makes almost exactly this point: to produce a desired change one applies the appropriate force, through the appropriate medium, to the appropriate object. His own examples include writing, printers, publishers and booksellers.

Thus:

A bank account can be a magical instrument.
A Hindi textbook can be a magical instrument.
A strength session can be a magical operation.
A flight to Uttarakhand can be a magical operation.

The test is not whether an action looks occult.

The test is whether it participates coherently in the Will.

VII. THE CREATIVE SEQUENCE

The complete operating sequence is:

