The experimenter returns to the prior identity without becoming psychologically dependent upon today's success or failure.

Then the cycle repeats.

VIII. WHY IMAGINATION IS CENTRAL

Tantric visualization is not well described as idle fantasy.

Sthaneshwar Timalsina's survey of classical tantric approaches describes imagination as a trainable power of the self that integrates attention, memory and intentional projection, and which can be developed into creative capacity.

This is critical.

The experiment does not train “thinking nice thoughts.”

It trains:

voluntary world-generation under sustained attention.

The distinction is:

Fantasy

The mind jumps between rewarding representations.

Bhāvanā

A selected experiential configuration is systematically cultivated until it becomes stable, embodied and cognitively consequential.

Hence the quality of visualization matters more than its flamboyance.

IX. FIRST-PERSON, NOT CINEMATIC

The target should rarely be visualized as a movie about the future self.

Instead:

be located inside him.

Do not watch yourself walking across the property.

Feel your feet walking across it.

Do not picture yourself speaking Hindi.

Hear the other person's reply from your own spatial perspective.

Do not admire an imagined dog.

Feel its weight against your leg.

Do not picture “having cows.”

Experience the inconvenience of needing to go outside because something actually needs feeding.

The target needs to migrate from:

desired object

toward:

normal phenomenal environment.

X. RASA: VISUALIZE THE TASTE OF THE WORLD

The physical scene is not the deepest target.

Its rasa is.

For the present experiment, the probable invariant is something like:

rootedness
autonomy
quiet competence
stewardship
animals
land
Indian belonging
scholarship
contemplation
simplicity
physical capability
freedom from institutional dependence

Different scenes instantiate the same attractor.

One night: monsoon.

Another: feeding animals.

Another: writing in the afternoon.

Another: talking to somebody locally in Hindi.

Another: fixing something broken.

Another: dealing with a veterinarian.

Another: paying a farm bill.

Another: a cold morning.

Another: an animal is ill and you respond competently.

This is crucial.

The target world must include maintenance, inconvenience and responsibility, otherwise you are training attraction toward a tourist advertisement rather than identity with the life itself.

The question after visualization is:

Did I merely see the objects, or did I taste the life?

XI. SETH: BELIEF AS WORLD-ORGANIZATION

Seth's model adds an important mechanism:

belief organizes perception, imagination, emotion and expectation.

The contemporary Seth Center still presents the core teaching as “you create your own reality,” and describes imagination as connecting probable events, beliefs and physical materialization.

The operational contribution is therefore:

The Belief Audit

Whenever a desired world feels implausible, ask:

What proposition am I presently treating as true that makes this world feel unavailable?

Examples:

“I will never make enough money.”

“A foreigner cannot build a real life there.”

“I don't have enough practical competence.”

“I always lose focus.”

Do not immediately counter with a positive slogan.

Investigate the belief.

Ask:

Where did it come from?
What evidence actually supports it?
What evidence contradicts it?
What behavior does believing it produce?
What replacement belief is both generative and presently credible?

Then rehearse the replacement with imagery and behavior.

XII. BASHAR: THE OPERATIONAL SEQUENCE

Bashar supplies one of the clearest manifestation algorithms:

vision → desire → belief → acceptance → intention → action → allowance.

Its most valuable addition is the final contradiction:

maximum engagement with minimum insistence.

His “excitement” formula says to act on the highest available excitement, take it as far as possible, and avoid insisting upon a predetermined result.

Translate this rigorously:

Excitement is not sovereign.

It is a ranking heuristic.

Among actions that:

are ethical;
satisfy current obligations;
plausibly serve the frozen trajectory;

prefer the one carrying the greatest authentic energy.

Then exhaust it.

When it stops opening, choose again.

This gives the experiment a local navigation function without allowing every impulse to redefine True Will.

XIII. CROWLEY: TRUE WILL

“Do what thou wilt” is not permission to obey every desire.

Crowley's explanation is the opposite:

discover the actual Will and cease wasting energy on trajectories inconsistent with it.

He explicitly distinguishes True Will from “do what you like” and joins one-pointedness with freedom from “lust of result.”

This supplies the experiment with a severe rule:

THE ONE-WILL RULE

The terminal world is not one hobby among twenty.

It becomes an organizing attractor.

Before a substantial commitment ask:

Does this strengthen, weaken or leave unchanged my trajectory toward the life I have chosen?

This does not require monomania.

Friendship, enjoyment, scholarship, travel and love may increase the person capable of living the target.

But years of activity that neither enrich life intrinsically nor increase target probability should become increasingly difficult to justify.

XIV. PAUL SELIG: IDENTITY PRECEDES CREATION

Selig's Guides repeatedly put identity before manifestation:

“I know who I am. I know what I am. I know how I serve.”

They explicitly instruct the practitioner to claim divine identity rather than allowing the frightened small self to occupy the governing position.

This maps almost perfectly onto Recognition if stripped of vocabulary differences.

Thus the sequence is not:

Goal → beg metaphysical power → receive goal.

It is:

Recognition → identity congruence → changed valuation → changed action → changed expression.

The Śaiva version is:

I am Śiva—not because this biography possesses cosmic omnipotence, but because the awareness appearing as this limited standpoint is not made from something outside Śiva.

Then:

How does Śiva-as-this-aperture act now?

That is a much more interesting daily question than an affirmation.

XV. RA: KNOW, ACCEPT, BECOME

The Law of One offers another striking parallel.

Its discipline of personality is summarized as:

know yourself → accept yourself → become the Creator.

It also treats visualization as deliberate training of concentrative power and says desire, will and polarity are key factors in magical work.

Its contribution to this protocol is twofold.

First: concentration itself must be trained.

If you cannot maintain an image voluntarily, the imagination is not yet a reliable instrument.

Second: power requires orientation.

Ask not only:

What do I want?

Ask:

What does this life make possible through me?

The target becomes stronger if the farm/hermitage is simultaneously:

home
research environment
ecological stewardship
animal care
scholarly base
place of contemplative practice
source of useful work

rather than simply private possession.

XVI. CASSIOPAEA: THE ADVERSARIAL CONTROL

Cassiopaean material is useful precisely because it mistrusts naive wishing.

Its “non-anticipation” discussion distinguishes intent from anxious projection of a future deficiency and argues for acting now with direction while releasing fixation on the mechanism or reward.

Its recurring “knowledge protects” principle adds the second half:

do not let metaphysics destroy discernment.

Every weekly review therefore includes:

THE CASSIOPAEA AUDIT

Where did I confuse:

desire with evidence?
coincidence with causation?
intensity with truth?
imagination with perception?
hope with prediction?
an intuitive impression with an instruction?

The stronger the manifestation hypothesis becomes, the more important this audit becomes.

XVII. ROWE: THE IMAGE MUST SOMETIMES ESCAPE YOU

Benjamin Rowe's Short Course in Scrying progresses through:

relaxation → concentration → sacred/refuge space → imaginal body → “surprise me” → pathworking → testing visions.

This introduces the second type of imagination.

Generative mode

You construct the target deliberately.

Receptive mode

You stop constructing.

Ask a question.

Then:

Surprise me.

Whatever follows is recorded.

Not believed.

Recorded.

Questions for receptive sessions:

What did I misunderstand about reaching this life?

What capability is future-me relying upon that I am ignoring?

What currently consumes energy that eventually disappeared?

What nearly prevented this?

What should tomorrow's bridge action be?

Over time measure whether the autonomous material predicts anything useful.

XVIII. CORBIN: IMAGINARY VS IMAGINAL

Henry Corbin's mundus imaginalis is valuable because it refuses the binary:

physical fact OR meaningless fantasy.

His imaginal framework treats active imagination as a mode through which structured symbolic experience may disclose itself.

For this experiment that remains a hypothesis, but it gives a useful phenomenological taxonomy.

Classify imagery as:

AUTHORED — deliberately constructed.

ASSOCIATIVE — obviously arising from memory/association.

AUTONOMOUS — appeared with unexpected organization.

NUMINOUS — unusually powerful or self-authenticating phenomenology.

VERIDICAL-CANDIDATE — contained a specific independently checkable claim.

Only the last category can ever become evidence of information acquisition beyond ordinary imaginative mechanisms, and only after independent verification.

Everything else remains phenomenology.

XIX. MONROE, KEPPLE AND ZIEWE: DENSITY AS TRAINING

The Monroe Institute explicitly describes Focus 12 “One Month Patterning” as an exercise intended to reshape one's life in a desired direction.

Frank Kepple goes substantially further, proposing that Focus 2 contains individually generated probability structures which may subsequently be “inserted” into Focus 1 physical experience. This is a metaphysical model, not an established scientific result, but it maps directly onto the strong version of this experiment.

Jürgen Ziewe's work is especially valuable methodologically because his explicit slogan is “awareness instead of belief”: direct exploration is privileged over inherited doctrine.

Therefore the OBE corpus contributes:

If imagination responds faster in less constrained phenomenal environments and physical reality responds more slowly, density can be interpreted as the environment in which intention encounters durable constraint and therefore generates learning.

Whether that metaphysical explanation is literally true is part of the experiment.

But its practical consequence is excellent:

Do not resent delay.

Delay exposes:

incoherent desire;
missing skills;
conflicting behavior;
insufficient resources;
fantasy;
impatience;
attachment;
lack of practical knowledge.

Instant manifestation could conceal all of these.

A slow world provides error correction.

XX. KABBALAH: KAVVANAH

Do not flatten Kabbalah into Law of Attraction.

The useful operational parallel is kavvanah:

directed intention embodied in actual contemplative/ritual action.

Scholarship on medieval Kabbalah explicitly treats human intention and action as theurgical—the practitioner participates through focused contemplative conduct rather than merely wanting something.

Its structural cosmology also supplies an intriguing comparison:

infinity → differentiation → finite articulation

versus:

Śiva → self-limitation → finite aperture.

They are not historically identical doctrines.

They are useful comparative structures.

XXI. THE DAIMON

The Re-rendering Atlas already gives the daimon practice a strong practical architecture:

oath → invocation → repetition → union → charge → dream incubation → log → staged deepening.

Its current Daimon page prescribes dawn, noon and dusk practice; repeated invocation; union; charge; dream-seeding; immediate dream recording; and links a staged Acher system with broader Proclean, Iamblichean, Synesian and Corbinian syntheses.

For this experiment, however, the Daimon is not given executive authority.

It is treated through three simultaneous interpretations:

H-D1 — psychological

A personification of unconscious/tacit cognition.

H-D2 — inexternalist

A relatively autonomous organization appearing intrinsically through the aperture while belonging to a larger process than ordinary egoic cognition.

H-D3 — strong imaginal/metaphysical

An independently structured intelligence encountered through imaginal mediation.

No interpretation is preselected.

And one rule is absolute:

NO PACTS

No bargain.

No surrender of autonomy.

No “if you give me the farm, I will…”

No obedience to commands merely because they appear numinous.

No entity receives ownership of the Will.

Information may be received.

It remains subject to judgement.

XXII. THE DAILY RULE OF LIFE

This is the rigid core.

Do this whether inspired or bored.

MORNING — 15 MINUTES
1. Recognition — 3 min

Sit.

Let visual, auditory and bodily experience appear.

Notice that thoughts about “me” are themselves appearing.

Then make the shift:

Localization is present. Separation is not thereby established.

Then:

I am Śiva here.

Do not strain to believe it.

Investigate what changes phenomenologically when it is entertained as the governing recognition.

2. Read the frozen target — 1 min

Do not modify it.

3. Invoke the rasa — 3 min

Do not picture possessions yet.

Remember the world-feeling.

Rootedness.

Freedom.

Land.

Animals.

Competence.

Study.

Silence.

Belonging.

4. Select today's kriyā — 3 min

Ask:

What single action today most increases the probability of the target world?

Write it.

It must be objectively completable.

5. Identity rehearsal — 3 min

Ask:

What would the version of me for whom this trajectory is ordinary do differently today?

Choose one behavior.

6. Release — 2 min

No demand for signs.

Begin the day.

