XXVI. DREAM INCUBATION

Two nights per week maximum.

Before sleep write one question.

Examples:

Show me what I am refusing to see about this trajectory.

What capability needs cultivation?

What is the next relevant obstacle?

Do not write:

Give me a prophetic dream proving manifestation is real.

On waking record immediately:

dream;
affect;
symbols;
spontaneous interpretation;
later interpretation;
any checkable prediction.

Keep them separate.

This adopts the dream-seeding/logging architecture already present in the Atlas daimon practice without precommitting to the source of the dreams.

XXVII. CONCENTRATION TRAINING

Three times weekly:

10 minutes.

Choose one simple image.

Circle.

Flame.

Red triangle.

Flower.

Hold it.

Whenever it collapses, restore it.

The purpose is not mystical experience.

The purpose is increasing voluntary stability of the imaginal field.

Ra explicitly treats this type of visualization as training for sustained inner concentration.

Rowe likewise puts concentration before advanced scrying.

XXVIII. THE WEEKLY AI REVIEW

Once each week conduct a 60–90 minute AI interview.

The AI receives:

frozen target;
seven nightly records;
daily adherence;
objective actions;
metrics;
predictions;
prior weekly synthesis;
current obstacles.

It interviews rather than lectures.

One question at a time.

The mandatory domains are:

1. Phenomenology

What changed in visualization, recognition, mood, dreams and identity?

2. Kriyā

What physically happened because you acted?

3. Avoidance

What important action was repeatedly postponed?

4. Belief

What belief produced the week's largest behavioral constraint?

5. Opportunity

What did you notice this week that earlier versions of you might have ignored?

6. Anomaly

Did anything genuinely surprising occur?

7. Alternative explanation

What is the strongest ordinary explanation?

8. Anticipation

Where were you compulsively checking whether “manifestation” was working?

9. Will

Did your desire for the frozen target remain coherent?

10. Bridge

What are next week's three highest-leverage physical moves?

The AI is explicitly instructed:

Do not reward metaphysical interpretations. Reward precision.

XXIX. THE EVENT CLASSIFIER

Every apparently meaningful event receives one classification.

C0 — ordinary background event

No plausible relationship.

C1 — direct causation

The event occurred because of an obvious action.

Example:

You emailed someone about land and received a contact.

C2 — salience-mediated opportunity

The opportunity probably existed independently, but goal orientation caused you to notice/use it.

C3 — coincidence

Relevant-looking event with no demonstrated causal relation.

C4 — pre-registered anomaly

A low-base-rate, specific event that matched something recorded before occurrence.

C5 — potentially anomalous information

Specific information received in a dream/scrying session and independently verified afterward, with ordinary information leakage investigated.

Only C4/C5 belong in the strong-metaphysics evidence ledger.

Everything else may still be useful.

XXX. PRE-REGISTRATION

Before running a specific metaphysical test:

write the prediction.

Example:

During the next 30 days I predict X.

Timestamp it.

Specify what would count.

Specify what would not count.

Then do not edit it.

This prevents symbolic elasticity from turning everything into confirmation.

XXXI. OPTIONAL SEXUAL-DISCIPLINE EXPERIMENT

Sexual restraint has traditional rationales in several yogic, tantric, brahmacarya and Daoist systems, but modern claims about semen retention are frequently much stronger than available biomedical evidence.

Therefore do not make it dogma.

Make it an experiment.

Choose a fixed period:

30 / 60 / 90 days.

Pre-register the rule:

pornography?
masturbation?
casual sexual fantasy deliberately indulged?
partnered sex?
ejaculation?

Then measure:

concentration;
intrusive sexual thought;
mood;
irritability;
sleep;
motivation;
work output;
meditation stability;
visualization vividness;
social confidence.

At completion compare against baseline.

If it improves the aperture's coherence, retain it.

If it merely produces agitation and obsessive suppression, modify it.

Ra's advice about desire is relevant here: desires are to be understood and integrated rather than merely “overcome” through repression.

XXXII. THE MONTHLY PATTERNING SESSION

Once monthly conduct a longer 45–60 minute session inspired partly by Monroe's One Month Patterning.

Monroe Institute describes that exercise explicitly as using Focus 12 to “reshape your life in desired direction.”

Our version is more measurable.

Visualize the next month, not age 35.

See:

where you work;
what habits are normal;
what project moves;
how much money is saved/earned;
Hindi practice;
body training;
one social connection;
one piece of Dehradun intelligence;
one practical skill.

Then convert each image into a metric.

The metaphysical target remains distant.

The behavioral bridge becomes near.

XXXIII. THE QUARTERLY CHECKPOINT

Every 13 weeks produce a frozen report.

A. Adherence

Percentage of prescribed practices completed.

B. Objective movement

What measurable aspects of the target became more probable?

C. Capability

What can you now do that you could not do 13 weeks ago?

D. Resources

Money.

Skills.

Relationships.

Knowledge.

Health.

E. Phenomenology

Recognition depth.

Visualization stability.

Dream intensity.

Autonomous imagery.

F. Strong-hypothesis evidence

C4/C5 events only.

G. Counterevidence

Predictions that failed.

Practices that did nothing.

Beliefs contradicted by reality.

H. Course correction

Change methods.

Never silently modify the frozen terminal target.

