]

That should be trained explicitly.

XLIV. THE FINAL PRINCIPLE

Do not spend eight years trying to make a future become real.

That phenomenologically preserves:

future ≠ now.

Instead let the future function as an attractor that continuously reorganizes the present.

Every night:

inhabit it.

Every morning:

recognize.

Every day:

perform one piece of it.

Every week:

interrogate the trajectory.

Every quarter:

measure.

Every year:

judge.

Then return to the operation.

The strongest formulation is therefore:

Recognition reveals consciousness as more than the contracted self-position. Svātantrya names its freedom. Icchā gives that freedom direction. Bhāvanā renders the direction experientially determinate. Rasa makes it lived. Jñāna reveals the bridge. Kriyā incarnates it through the conditions of the world. Non-attachment leaves the route open. Feedback disciplines fantasy. Repeated recognition prevents the produced world from becoming a new bondage.

Or more simply:

I AM ŚIVA.
THIS IS THE WORLD I CHOOSE.
I INHABIT IT.
I LEARN WHAT IT REQUIRES.
I DO WHAT IT REQUIRES.
I DO NOT DICTATE HOW IT MUST ARRIVE.
I RECORD WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENS.

That is the experiment.

This is the version I would make canonical in Life90. The important change from v3 is that the entire interface can now be organized around this cycle—Recognition → Icchā → Bhāvanā → Rasa → Jñāna → Kriyā → Feedback—with each source becoming a methodology card rather than a loose “spiritual sources” section.